  {
   "unit": 21,
   "type": "scene",
   "label": "3D explorer",
   "title": "Wave plate: the two components drift apart",
   "points": [
    "Plane-polarised light (E at angle <b>θ</b> to the optic axis, which is along y) enters the plate. It splits into e (along y, green) and o (along z, coral).",
    "Set <b>phase difference δ</b>: a thicker plate lets the o component lag more. The amber curve at the right is the path of the emerging E-vector.",
    "Try θ = 45°: δ = 90° gives a circle (quarter-wave plate), δ = 180° gives a line turned through 2θ (half-wave plate).",
    "Other θ at δ = 90° gives an ellipse; δ = 0 or 360° leaves the light unchanged."
   ],
   "scene": {
    "camera": {
     "position": [
      6.5,
      2.6,
      5.2
     ],
     "target": [
